WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.310
- In April, we had the
Backstreet Boys here.

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.410
Obviously we had a lot to connect on,

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:05.970
especially when it comes to life on tour.

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:07.516
So check this out.

00:00:07.516 --> 00:00:08.647
(audience claps) - [Kelly] Wow.

00:00:08.647 --> 00:00:09.818
- Two baby girls, both born in Vegas.

00:00:09.818 --> 00:00:11.017
- [Howie] It's those cold winters.

00:00:11.017 --> 00:00:12.101
- [Kelly] Oh my God, congratulations.

00:00:12.101 --> 00:00:12.951
(laughs)

00:00:12.951 --> 00:00:14.670
Yeah, congratulations
though, that's exciting.

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:15.503
- Yeah.

00:00:15.503 --> 00:00:17.220
- So is that gonna be hard to like leave?

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:18.060
I mean, I know you get like,

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.530
it's nice because you
get to actually sleep

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:20.645
but, like

00:00:20.645 --> 00:00:22.260
(chuckles) I've had babies.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.600
But is it kind of hard
'cause they're so little?

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.800
- I mean, so my daughter

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.060
just turned 11 months old,

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.160
and my other daughter
is over two years old,

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.720
actually about to be three,

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.400
and yeah like I said,

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.810
we've had time back home with them,

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:36.450
and I've been driving them to school,

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.160
making them breakfast.
- That's so cool.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:38.993
- Like doing the whole
stay at home dad thing.

00:00:38.993 --> 00:00:40.200
And now, thankfully,

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.090
we have some shows coming up in Vegas

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:43.080
and that's where I live,

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.820
so basically I can just drive to work

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:46.290
and then go do my job. -
[Kelly] Oh, that's awesome.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:48.300
- [Howie] We take them with us
on tour in the summer times.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.700
It's like a National Lampoons Vacation.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:51.870
- [Kelly] Yeah, it's like all the kids,

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:53.043
like the whole bus. - It's like a convoy.

00:00:53.043 --> 00:00:53.876
- [Kevin] We each have our own bus

00:00:53.876 --> 00:00:55.693
and we all have our families on the buses.

00:00:55.693 --> 00:00:57.270
- [Kelly] - I was gonna
say, it has to be different

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:58.680
obviously when you start out.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:00:59.820
And it is a big thing,

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.410
people don't realize like...

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:02.243
You're on stage,

00:01:02.243 --> 00:01:03.660
your voice goes away when you're tired,

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:04.590
you have to get sleep.

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:06.390
But like even me, like
when I went on tour,

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:07.740
like after having my first kid,

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:10.140
I was like, 'cause I'm not like a,

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.090
I don't just like, let
someone else raise my kid.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.350
- [BSB] Right, yeah. -[Kevin] Absolutely.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:15.667
So it's like you are exhausted
when you get on stage.

00:01:15.667 --> 00:01:16.647
- [BSB] Totally.

00:01:16.647 --> 00:01:18.870
- But you get so much out
of it though too you know.

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:19.703
- [Kelly] Totally.

00:01:19.703 --> 00:01:21.480
Yeah, yeah. But it's one
of those things where

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:22.830
it was different to navigate.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:25.530
Like even shows and like my
kind of rituals beforehand,

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:26.820
and getting like my,

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:27.900
are y'all experiencing that?

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:29.250
Like how you're gonna prepare for that.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:31.170
'Cause it's a different
thing going in as parents.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:32.003
- [BSB] Absolutely.

00:01:32.003 --> 00:01:34.440
- Yeah I think we all have
different systems probably.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.068
You know, because I have
a soon-to-be 20 year old.

00:01:37.068 --> 00:01:38.231
- [Kelly] Yeah, oh my God,
I didn't realize that.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:39.064
- [Brian] Life is -

00:01:39.064 --> 00:01:40.754
- Oh my God, we're all old.

00:01:40.754 --> 00:01:42.685
- [AJ] I know right, ugh.

00:01:42.685 --> 00:01:43.602
Oh my gosh.

00:01:44.443 --> 00:01:45.780
- [Kelly] I can't even,
I didn't even know that.

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:47.250
- Yeah, he's in country music.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.710
- Oh, that's amazing. -
Yeah, it's a thing to,

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:51.210
I mean it's a lovely thing to watch but

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.043
- [Kelly] Yeah

00:01:52.043 --> 00:01:53.340
as I've seen these guys have kids too,

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:54.330
it's just kind of like,

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:55.530
Oh you're there now.

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:56.363
Haha!

00:01:56.363 --> 00:01:57.240
- [AJ] Yeah.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:58.073
- Good luck with that.

00:01:58.073 --> 00:01:58.906
- Good luck with it.

00:01:58.906 --> 00:02:01.140
- It is so difficult, but
it is worth it though.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:03.240
'cause it is cool to be
able to be at this place

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:04.710
in your career where you
can afford to like have

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:05.543
your whole family there,

00:02:05.543 --> 00:02:06.720
and you're not like struggling, you know.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:08.300
- We have amazing wives, honestly.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:10.543
They are truly the heart, backbone.

00:02:10.543 --> 00:02:11.376
- [Kevin] Yeah they hold it down.

00:02:11.376 --> 00:02:13.042
- Yeah they hold it down.
- [AJ] Rocks.

00:02:13.042 --> 00:02:15.870
- I have an amazing sister
wife, my nanny. She's amazing.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:17.130
I call her my sister wife.

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:18.330
I'm like, she's awesome.

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:20.670
It is, you can't do your
job without having help.

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:22.080
And it's a beautiful thing to

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.790
have somebody that you love and trust

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:24.870
with your children.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:25.703
- Totally - [Kelly] An awesome thing.

00:02:25.703 --> 00:02:26.536
- [Howie] I was gonna say
it's kind of cool though.

00:02:26.536 --> 00:02:27.660
'cause when we first
started in this business

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.520
almost 30 years ago.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:30.960
We were just young kids you know.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:32.520
We were like kids in a candy store

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:33.688
just seeing the world.

00:02:33.688 --> 00:02:34.521
- Yeah.

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:35.880
- And I think like now
looking back to where,

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.470
how it started and you know,

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:39.930
over time sometimes the freshness

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.310
kind of goes a little bit stale.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:42.450
But bringing our kids out,

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:44.220
and them actually get a
chance to see the world,

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.330
and seeing it through their eyes.

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:46.163
- Yeah.

00:02:46.163 --> 00:02:47.070
- Constantly keeps it fresh for us.

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:48.120
- Absolutely.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:48.953
That's the thing with kids,

00:02:48.953 --> 00:02:50.310
everything is kind of
brand new for you again,

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:51.540
because you're like seeing
it through their eyes.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:52.373
It's really cool.

00:02:52.373 --> 00:02:53.220
I wanna come back wait.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:54.510
Did you say your kid is in country music?

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:55.556
Is that what you were saying down?

00:02:55.556 --> 00:02:56.389
- [Brian] Yeah.

00:02:56.389 --> 00:02:57.222
He's in country music.

00:02:57.222 --> 00:02:58.080
- [Kelly] Okay wait,

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.100
We should just get him on.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:00.163
I love country music.

00:03:00.163 --> 00:03:01.050
I just didn't know that,

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:02.850
now I'm very much into this.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:03.683
- [Brian] Okay.

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:05.310
Well you have your people call my people.

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:07.721
- Okay I will. - [Brian] There you go.

00:03:07.721 --> 00:03:09.450
- [Kelly] I'll like make the
plane and fly it down to you.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:10.977
- [AJ] Yeah. -[Brian] Thank you.

00:03:10.977 --> 00:03:12.660
- No, that's so cool, that's exciting.

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:14.490
As a parent, like you're
in the music world,

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:16.350
and for your kid to kind of go
into the music world as well.

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:17.673
That's really flattering.

00:03:18.769 --> 00:03:19.602
- [BSB] He's really talented.

00:03:19.602 --> 00:03:20.490
- [BSB] He's a great talent.
- It's great to watch.

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:23.400
he started on Broadway in
New York when he was 12.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:24.360
- Wow.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:27.240
- So he's a, I mean, this
is all he knows, you know

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.950
that's the thing, that's
a blessing about it.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:29.790
He's like dad, I don't know

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:31.490
if I could work a normal job like,

00:03:32.895 --> 00:03:36.180
because during COVID he
wrote like 200 songs.

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:37.545
- Well there was a lot of time, right.

00:03:37.545 --> 00:03:38.760
- [Brian] Yeah there was a lot of time.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.650
So, but I'm just super proud,

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.330
like we all are super proud of our kids

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:44.193
- [Kelly] Oh that's so cool.

